The Lojbanic ['] is usually pronounced like the English h...
not like the Scottish ch or either the hard or soft ch of
German or the Greek version(s).

Imagine a cold winter day where you want to make a cloud
of you breath -- that is the approximate consonant you
would use. The throat is fully open and relaxed, as are
the lips -- there is no constriction, and no real motion
of the glottis or uvula or lips or tongue. It's a simple
puff of air through an open pipe.

Does that help any?


